---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';

const site = 'https://bla5k.com';

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    name: 'About bla5k',
    description: 'Who writes and reviews bla5k — the editorial team, our review process, and how we keep the directory trustworthy.',
    url: `${site}/about/`,
    mainEntity: { '@id': `${site}/#org` },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${site}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: `${site}/about/` },
    ],
  },
];
---
<Page
  title="About bla5k — The Editorial Team & How We Review Tools"
  heading="About bla5k"
  description="Meet the editorial team behind bla5k, read our review process, and see how every tool in the directory is verified before it's listed."
  schema={schema}
>
  <p>
    <strong>bla5k</strong> is a hand-organized directory of the internet's best tools,
    websites, and communities — reviewed and curated by people who care about what they
    recommend.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is behind bla5k</h2>
  <p>
    bla5k is an independent editorial project. Our team is small by design: every entry
    is reviewed and curated by a human before it earns a place in the directory. We cover
    four areas — <strong>tools &amp; software testing</strong>,{' '}
    <strong>product research</strong>, <strong>content editing</strong>, and{' '}
    <strong>site operations</strong> — and every review passes through at least one
    editor before publishing.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you'd like to know who reviewed a specific tool, every entry shows its publication
    and update dates, and you can always <a href="/contact/">ask us directly</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How we review tools (the process)</h2>
  <p>Every tool in the directory goes through the same four-step review:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>1. Verify what it claims.</strong> We check the product, its free tier, and what's actually paid — not just the marketing page.</li>
    <li><strong>2. Check pricing honestly.</strong> Free tier, hidden limits, message caps, watermarks, and upgrade pressure all get noted.</li>
    <li><strong>3. Compare alternatives.</strong> We place the tool against its closest competitors so you can see the trade-offs, not just the highlights.</li>
    <li><strong>4. Write it plainly.</strong> Each entry explains what the tool is in simple words, who it's for, and who it isn't for.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Listings that fail verification — broken signup, misleading pricing, or a dead product —
    are removed or flagged rather than published. That's why the directory is smaller
    than it could be, and why you can trust what's in it.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
  <p>
    bla5k is funded independently. Our editorial content is never sold: a paid placement
    is always visibly labeled <strong>Sponsored</strong> and can never change a rating, a
    review, or how a tool is covered. The ★ editor's pick badge is earned, not bought.
    Our <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure page</a> documents this in full, and our{' '}
    <a href="/advertise/">Advertise page</a> shows exactly what a paid placement means —
    and doesn't mean.
  </p>

  <h2>How we keep things accurate</h2>
  <p>
    Tools change constantly, and we update entries as products evolve. If you spot
    something out of date — a changed price, a broken feature, a tool we missed — tell us
    via the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page. Corrections are handled quickly:
    verified factual errors are fixed, and significant changes are logged on the entry's
    update date.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We don't list sites that distribute pirated or copyright-infringing content.</li>
    <li>We don't accept payment to change a review, rating, or ranking.</li>
    <li>We don't publish reviews we haven't verified, and we never present untested claims as our own experience.</li>
    <li>We don't claim to be affiliated with any tool we review — the directory is independent.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our policies</h2>
  <p>
    bla5k is built on transparency. Here are the policies that govern the site:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> — how we collect, use, and protect your data.</li>
    <li><a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a> — the rules governing your use of bla5k.</li>
    <li><a href="/dmca/">DMCA &amp; Copyright Policy</a> — copyright and takedown procedure.</li>
    <li><a href="/disclosure/">Affiliate &amp; Advertising Disclosure</a> — how bla5k is supported.</li>
    <li><a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> — cookie usage and GDPR consent.</li>
    <li><a href="/acceptable-use/">Acceptable Use Policy</a> — what's allowed on the site.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Have a tool we should include, or spotted something out of date? We'd love to hear
    from you — head to the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
  </p>
</Page>
